by Tony Bennett or Andy Williams.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"A History of Rock Music in 500 Songs","episode":"Episode 68: \"Yakety Yak\" by the Coasters","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dtMHDD0-oOo"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Vocal Style Avoiding Malisma","body":"Tony Bennett is identified as one of the notable vocalists from the first half of the 20th century who adhered to the practice of singing one note per syllable, hitting each note precisely without excessive ornamentation, consistent with the prevailing definition of good singing at the time. \"If you listen to any of the great voices of the first part of the 20th century, Sinatra, Bing Crosby, Tony Bennett, they will almost without exception hit the note dead arm, one note per syllable.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"A History of Rock Music in 500 Songs","episode":"Episode 32: \"I Got A Woman\" by Ray Charles","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0oeI9f2x_fo"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":38227452650766,"type":"song","name":"Stranger in Paradise","work_year":1954,"list_id":2117123013911,"list":"Billboard Year-End 1954","src":"singles","rank":19,"year":1954,"note":"","yt":"BqecjMVNZKY","scaruffi":null},{"id":38227452650766,"type":"song","name":"Stranger in Paradise","work_year":1954,"list_id":132335824845498,"list":"Billboard Year-End Hot 100","src":"charts","rank":19,"year":1954,"note":null,"yt":"BqecjMVNZKY","scaruffi":null},{"id":38227452650766,"type":"song","name":"Stranger in Paradise","work_year":1954,"list_id":95472960493301,"list":"UK nº1 · 1950s","src":"singles","rank":32,"year":1955,"note":"2 semanas","yt":"BqecjMVNZKY","scaruffi":null},{"id":191396959647802,"type":"album","name":"I Left My Heart in San Francisco","list_id":85122334056025,"list":"Grammy Award: Album of the Year nominees","src":"musthear","rank":1963,"year":1962,"note":null,"yt":"3T7TChwZ47o","scaruffi":null},{"id":191396959647802,"type":"album","name":"I Left